    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` behavior for `POST /api/owners` following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**Behavior**: When a create request sets `sharesHousehold: true` and an existing owner already shares its household (same last name + address, compared case-insensitively with whitespace collapsed), the request is allowed and both the new owner and the existing member(s) are assigned the same stable `householdId`, which is returned on the owner. Without the flag, a household duplicate is still rejected with 409 (unchanged).\n\n**Changes**:\n- **`OwnerHouseholds.java`** (new package-private helper) \u2014 the single definition of household membership (`members(...)`) and the stable id derivation (`householdId(...)`, a 12-char hex prefix of SHA-256 over the canonical last name + address, so every member computes the same value regardless of creation order). This removes the `canonical`/matching logic that was duplicated in the reject step.\n- **`RejectDuplicateOwnerHousehold.java`** \u2014 refactored to delegate membership detection to `OwnerHouseholds`.\n- **`AssignOwnerHousehold.java`** (new function) \u2014 when opted in and a household exists, assigns the shared id to the built owner and persists it onto existing members lacking it. Wired into `owners.POST.yml` as a new `assignHousehold` step after `assignCustomerCode`, under the same transaction.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `household_id` persisted field with accessors.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `householdId` as a read-only field on the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it on the response).\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 ignore `householdId` when mapping the request DTO to an entity (consistent with `customerCode`).\n- **schema.sql** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `household_id` column.\n\nI also fixed a latent bug in the id derivation: `String.format(\"%02X\", digest[i])` sign-extends negative bytes, so I masked with `& 0xFF`.\n\nThe dedicated acceptance test (`coreJoinersShareHouseholdId`) and the full `./mvnw test` suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
